{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Before the [Eb]hills, before the [Cm]sea, before the [Ab]dawn [Bb]of [Eb]days
The Word [Cm]was there with God, and he [Ab]was God in all [Bb]his ways
[Ab]All things came in[Bb]to being through [Eb]him, [Bb/D]not one thing a[Cm]part
In [Ab]him was life, and that [Bb]life was the light of ev[Eb]ery heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In the beginning was the Word
And the [Abmaj7]Word was with [Bb]God, and the [Cm]Word was [Ab]God
The [Eb]light shines in the [Bb]darkness
And the [Ab]darkness [Bb]has not over[Eb]come it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There came a man sent from God, [Cm]and John was his name
To tes[Ab]tify about [Bb]the light, [Eb]a witness, so [Bb]he came
The [Cm]true light came into the world [Ab]that through him came [Bb]to be
[Ab]The world did not know him, and [Bb]his own would not [Eb]receive
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ebmaj7/D]But to [Cm]all who did receive him, who be[Ab]lieved in his name
He [Eb]gave the right to become chil[Bb]dren of God
Not born of [Cm]blood or human will, but [Ab]born of God above
Held [Eb]in the Father's mercy and [Bb]carried in his love
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In the beginning was the [Eb]Word
And the [Ab]Word was with [Bb]God, and the [Cm]Word was [Ab]God
The [Eb]light shines in the [Bb]darkness
And the [Ab]darkness [Bb]has not over[Eb]come it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
And the [Ab]Word became [Eb]flesh and made his [Bb]dwelling among [Cm]us
And [Ab]we have seen [Eb]his glory
The [Bb]glory of the Father's only [Ab]Son
Full of grace and [Eb]truth
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Ab]Word be[Bb]came [Cm]flesh
[Ab]Full of grace [Bb]and truth
